> "We should make something together!"

This was my enthusiastic response to my good mate Craig Parker, as he was driving us to the Thought Bubble Comic Festival in 2024. 

We were idly chatting about his frustration with a really cool story idea which he was recently tinkering with. I was 6 pages into writing and drawing my first comic and was having a short break before plowing on. So I tuned to him and suggested that we could do something together - me drawing and him writing - just to get something out there and done. 

After willingly handing over hundred of pounds between us on amazing art at Thought Bubble we walked away further inspired and enthused to do something ourselves. But what, we weren't sure. 

We met several weeks later to discuss some ideas concepts that Craig had come up with. We agreed early on at that we should start really small and keep it only 5/6 pages long as we were both still finding our feet with the form - as well as the the fact that we have full-time jobs and lives. 

After that chat I went away and started sketching some early ideas. 

We talked through the initial script. 

[ealy sketch ideas]

I decided early on that I wanted to colour this one. This is a bih stretch for me as I've always steered away from colouring. 

I learned a lot from this experience. I realised that you reallly need to think about colouring at the inking or even the penciling stage. 

Now let me tell you what a delight it is to make cool things with your mates. It's one of lifes great joys. 
